directed graph’s simple graph once, lazily, each in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"vertices"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"order (by vertex index): an isolated vertex, or one whose only edges are loops, is a clique of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"one. The order is Eppstein–Löffler–Strash’s: by the cliques’ first vertex in"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"coreNumbers().degeneracyOrdering"},{"type":"text","text":", then as Bron–Kerbosch with Tomita’s pivot (ties to the least"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"index) and branches in ascending index meets them. The sequence holds the graph, so iterating"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"again gives the same cliques. O(n + m) before the first clique, O(d·n·3^(d\/3)) in all for"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"degeneracy d."}],"role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"MaximalCliques","kind":"identifier"}]},"doc://Cliques/documentation/Cliques":{"kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Cliques\/documentation\/Cliques","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/cliques","abstract":[],"role":"collection","title":"Cliques"},"doc://Cliques/documentation/Cliques/MaximalCliques/starts(with:by:)":{"url":"\/documentation\/cliques\/maximalcliques\/starts(with:by:)","identifier":"doc:\/\/Cliques\/documentation\/Cliques\/MaximalCliques\/starts(with:by:)","type":"topic","kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","title":"starts(with:by:)","abstract":[],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"starts"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"genericParameter","text":"PossiblePrefix"},{"kind":"text","text":">("},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"with"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"PossiblePrefix","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"by","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": (","kind":"text"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":".","kind":